---v4/HANDOFF.md---
# CORE70 v4 — bodies complete, controller qualification HOLD

This is SOURCE/DATA preparation, not runtime authorization or acceptance.
All 70 IDs have concrete calls in three layouts (210 UNRUN cells). No product,
parser, matcher, Shell, Worker, compiler, install or native oracle ran here.
No production files changed. Earlier v1/v2/v3 evidence remains unchanged.

## Exact binding

- Candidate: `da4e1cc187022255521879b00db2ac77674f79d9`; all 305 selected source
  inputs authenticated by the successful DATA builder.
- Complete package: 1002 members, 908381 compressed bytes,
  SHA256 `4f90df04dba998f184473254bb450f9e085b9fc9d5994dc91a21a7ccf1d1d66e`.
  Retained compressed bytes reauthenticated; no inflation in this phase.
- Compiled manifest: `f42f0008bf5939f28ccb7cd038b9f462a03efa38238709c97a7daab7c98e3035`.
- Execution seal: `ea3c82e4192729f4cbd2172e9548d5e21da3d4e3d8ccbfbfa7ad591a47736301`.
  This seals preparation bytes, NOT successful controller qualification.
- New isolated root: `/private/tmp/safe-bash-core70-v4-20260829`.
  Source-built, installed and physically moved layouts retain authenticated
  candidate members; the moved origin is absent. No live HEAD substitution.

## Completed authoring, not observed behavior

`CASES-v4.json` maps the unchanged 32 references, 8 H protocols, EC01–25 and
EH01–05 to the exact 210 layout cells. `cell-v4.mjs`, `host-bodies.mjs` and the
copied additions provide actual bodies, not deferred placeholder dispatches.

- H02: fixed forwarding checkpoint Worker wrapper, one filtered own-data
  witness, object and false caller reasons; actual work/checkpoint forwarding.
- H03: real `maxExpansionBytes:1` with payload `aa` and zero-Worker assertion;
  reachable group/node/interval limits and private pattern/work/state cases.
  Work/state exhaustion expectations remain source-derived and UNRUN.
- H04: forwarding reserve/hold/close and retain/release observers, actual
  snapshot retention/replacement, failed-reservation atomicity and cleanup.
- H05: exactly-one retained-argument postMessage gate after genuine invoke;
  readonly, stale/local-restoration and caller variants, without state injection.
- H07: fixed production-entry to authenticated owned fault entries with
  unchanged Worker options; malformed replies, positive companions and restore.
- H06: standalone exact-false sink, independent of caller abort. H08: fresh
  initial allowance equality. EH04/EH05 retain concrete cleanup/error and exact
  invoke-Promise versus derived/thenable checks. Raw-falsy terminal presence is
  implemented explicitly, not inferred from truthiness.
- EH01/EH02 v4 use an environment pattern of 65537 ASCII bytes against the
  genuine private pattern cap 65536, preserving the ordinary source-byte limit.
  The old 33-group unsupported-grammar stimulus is not a private status3 proof.

H02/H04/H05/H07 are TEST-ONLY instrumented profiles, not stock runtime evidence.
All wrappers, fixed paths, options and whole private closure are sealed. There
is no arbitrary URL, public test seam, counter injection or lowered limit.

## Explicit unresolved proof qualifications

H03 depth64 is SOURCE_ONLY: recursive group entry is dominated by the earlier
32-group guard. It is not an executed depth-limit branch. H04 MAX_SAFE ticket
exhaustion is SOURCE_ONLY. Registered host cleanup rejection does not prove an
actual private ArrayOwner.close rejection; that private failure remains
unobserved, not substituted by a host cleanup assertion. These qualifications
must be reviewed explicitly; authored bodies are not proof of all their claims.

## Actual preparation results and failures

Four PURE/controller processes were used: inspection exited0; original builder
exited1 on an exact source-anchor mismatch; versioned builder exited0; final
controller exited1 before control execution. All four process exits returned
